      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collection/extraction_schema/0/description",
      "value": "Classify the latest turn against the actual last assistant question and full dialogue. Yes to May I help you first or to continuing assistance after a failed transfer is assist_yes, never accept or support_yes. No to the initial help-first question is human; no to continuing after a failed transfer is assist_no. An unqualified yes to the current payment offer/read-back is accept. Corrected dates/amounts, including yes but, are proposal. A payment date or amount proposal is never refusal. Vague payment periods and continued lack of an exact day after clarification are vague_date. Unrelated non-answers and no to today without a proposal are refusal. Full amount too much is full_too_much; rejection of the offered floor, including that is still too much, is refusal. In a support-offer question, yes/no is support_yes/support_no. Human insistence is human. Paid means payment of this past-due amount; historical payoff/closure or product denial is dispute. Hardship with a voluntarily supplied date or amount is proposal and also sets hardship_signal=yes. Refusal to talk is stop. Never infer a tool success."
